# An unknown head with a known method's application as its tail defines a named Structure and
# calls nothing (Q58; the author, 2026-10-05; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#construction): `t: shout()`
# retains shout's application in its body without executing it; `s: shout` binds s to shout's
# occurrence (K03 NS-ROLES-1b) and runs nothing either, so shout prints nothing.
# report prints DONE (a C door keeps it native when the root is walked) and gives 7.
# The program says only DONE. Entry 7.
fn: shout () int
    c.printf: "called\n"
    return: 1

fn: report () int
    c.printf: "DONE\n"
    return: 7
end: report

s: shout
t: shout()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: report(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
